sign-digest-hmac-scheme: TPM2_SignDigest rejects a key whose scheme is TPM_ALG_HMAC

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 3 (version 185), "TPM2_SignDigest",
"General Description"):

  "The scheme of keyHandle must be a signing scheme that supports signing a
  digest (e.g., TPM_ALG_ECDSA, but not TPM_ALG_HMAC)."

Part 3, Table "Signing commands overview": HMAC with TPM2_SignDigest() /
TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature() is "Not supported".

TPM2_SignDigest accepts any scheme that CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme()
accepts, so a keyed-hash key with scheme TPM_ALG_HMAC produces an HMAC of the
digest. The command now returns TPM_RC_SCHEME + RC_SignDigest_keyHandle for
it, as in tpm-rs.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c
@@ -124,6 +124,13 @@ TPM2_SignDigest(SignDigest_In*  in,  // IN: input parameter list
             return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_SignDigest_keyHandle;
         }
     }
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // the scheme "must be a signing scheme that supports signing a digest (e.g.,
+    // TPM_ALG_ECDSA, but not TPM_ALG_HMAC)" (Part 3, TPM2_SignDigest).
+    if(objectScheme.scheme == TPM_ALG_HMAC)
+    {
+        return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_SignDigest_keyHandle;
+    }
     hashAlg = CryptoCommon_GetSignSchemeHashAlg(&objectScheme);
 
     // If validation is provided, or the key is restricted, check the ticket
